WEBVTT

00:00:34.159 --> 00:00:36.787
Mmm. Spider... Hubble...

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.871
Nitro...

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.581
Ooh! Big Pink!

00:00:39.665 --> 00:00:42.584
It's the only gum
with the breath-freshening power of ham.

00:00:42.668 --> 00:00:45.295
And it pinkens your teeth while you chew.

00:00:46.355 --> 00:00:50.275
All right, sergeant, $100 worth
of Pixy Stix and porno mags

00:00:50.359 --> 00:00:53.487
with your five percent military discount
comes to $95.

00:00:56.949 --> 00:00:58.033
That'll be 40 cents.

00:00:58.116 --> 00:01:01.036
I believe you're forgetting
about our five percent military discount.

00:01:01.119 --> 00:01:03.956
- What's only for people in the military.
- What?

00:01:04.039 --> 00:01:06.416
This is the worst kind
of discrimination...

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.960
the kind against me.

00:01:08.043 --> 00:01:09.753
All right, look, our policy is

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.297
if for any reason
you're not completely satisfied,

00:01:12.381 --> 00:01:13.382
I hate you.

00:01:14.758 --> 00:01:15.759
- Hey, fellas...
- Whoa!

00:01:17.469 --> 00:01:19.054
Okay, now I'm mad.

00:01:20.931 --> 00:01:22.307
Full price for gum?

00:01:22.432 --> 00:01:24.726
That dog won't hunt, monsignor.

00:01:28.981 --> 00:01:29.982
Hello.

00:01:30.065 --> 00:01:31.858
We're here because we, uh...

00:01:32.442 --> 00:01:33.902
love our planet.

00:01:35.696 --> 00:01:39.574
Sign here on the dotted line, patriots,
and I'll give you your discount cards

00:01:39.658 --> 00:01:42.411
Just out of curiosity...
we can use the cards to buy gum

00:01:42.494 --> 00:01:44.413
then immediately quit the army, right?

00:01:44.496 --> 00:01:46.039
Playing you all for chumps?

00:01:46.123 --> 00:01:47.791
Correct. There's no obligation.

00:01:50.836 --> 00:01:53.505
Unless of course... war were declared.

00:01:54.089 --> 00:01:55.674
What's that?

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:57.843
War were declared.

00:02:06.935 --> 00:02:08.645
Now, be careful, Fry,

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:11.773
and if you kill anyone,
make sure to eat their heart

00:02:11.857 --> 00:02:13.400
to gain their courage...

00:02:13.483 --> 00:02:16.612
Their rich, tasty courage.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.905
I don't want you to worry about your jobs

00:02:18.989 --> 00:02:20.073
while you're away.

00:02:20.157 --> 00:02:21.658
That's why I'm firing you now.

00:02:23.952 --> 00:02:25.078
I want to enlist.

00:02:25.162 --> 00:02:27.748
My friends always die
if I'm not there to save them.

00:02:27.831 --> 00:02:31.084
Sorry, but the army's instituted
a men-only policy.

00:02:31.168 --> 00:02:33.211
- What?
- It's shameful, I agree.

00:02:33.295 --> 00:02:36.423
In the olden days, I proudly fought
alongside female troops

00:02:36.506 --> 00:02:39.259
shoulder to, uh... shoulder.

00:02:39.635 --> 00:02:41.887
Alas, after a series of deadly blunders

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.097
caused by distracting low-cut fatigues

00:02:44.181 --> 00:02:45.849
and lots of harmless pinching

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:48.518
the army decided women weren't fit
for service.

00:02:48.602 --> 00:02:50.020
Not when I'm in charge.

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:52.814
You know, Zapp, someone ought
to teach you a lesson.

00:02:52.898 --> 00:02:54.733
If it's a lesson in love, watch out.

00:02:54.816 --> 00:02:58.153
I suffer from a very sexy
learning disability.

00:02:58.236 --> 00:02:59.488
What do I call it, Kif?

00:02:59.571 --> 00:03:01.990
Sex-lexia.

00:03:12.751 --> 00:03:14.753
Men, you're lucky men.

00:03:14.836 --> 00:03:17.005
Soon you'll all be fighting
for your planet.

00:03:17.089 --> 00:03:19.216
Many of you will be dying for your planet.

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:22.052
A few of you will be forced
through a fine-meshed screen

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.178
for your planet.

00:03:23.261 --> 00:03:25.180
They will be the luckiest of all.

00:03:25.263 --> 00:03:26.890
Great. We're gonna die.

00:03:26.974 --> 00:03:29.309
And this ham gum is all bones.

00:03:30.269 --> 00:03:32.646
Now to present the logistics
of our mission

00:03:32.729 --> 00:03:34.231
the commander in chief.

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:36.900
Please welcome the original Gerber baby

00:03:36.984 --> 00:03:40.445
Earth president Richard M. Nixon.

00:03:41.655 --> 00:03:43.865
This is the brass ring, fellas.

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:47.160
Planet Spheron One.

00:03:47.244 --> 00:03:48.495
Cool effect!

00:03:48.578 --> 00:03:50.914
It's a desolate, ugly, little planet

00:03:50.998 --> 00:03:54.376
with absolutely no natural resources
or strategic value.

00:03:54.459 --> 00:03:55.460
Questions?

00:03:55.585 --> 00:03:58.672
Why is this godforsaken planet
worth dying for?

00:03:58.755 --> 00:04:01.383
Don't ask me. You're the one
who's going to be dying.

00:04:01.466 --> 00:04:03.760
Just so we'll know, who's the enemy?

00:04:03.844 --> 00:04:05.012
A valid question.

00:04:05.095 --> 00:04:06.930
We know nothing about their language

00:04:07.014 --> 00:04:09.016
their history, or what they look like

00:04:09.099 --> 00:04:10.809
but we can assume this...

00:04:10.892 --> 00:04:14.354
they stand for everything
we don't stand for.

00:04:14.438 --> 00:04:17.107
Also, they told me you guys
look like dorks.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.859
They look like dorks!

00:04:18.942 --> 00:04:20.027
I'm gonna...

00:04:37.502 --> 00:04:39.921
What's the matter, private?
Tent got your tongue?

00:04:40.255 --> 00:04:41.381
Tent got your...

00:04:41.465 --> 00:04:44.718
Kif, write that down
and send it to "Humor in Uniform."

00:04:50.849 --> 00:04:51.850
Hmm.

00:05:19.628 --> 00:05:21.463
Whoa! Check out that guy.

00:05:21.546 --> 00:05:24.508
He makes speedy Gonzales
look like regular Gonzales.

00:05:27.302 --> 00:05:29.680
That new recruit is phenomenal, sir.

00:05:29.763 --> 00:05:32.975
Yes. He edged out my old Mark
by two seconds.

00:05:33.308 --> 00:05:34.685
And 16 minutes.

00:05:34.935 --> 00:05:36.561
And 12 hours.

00:05:36.979 --> 00:05:39.022
I do plan to finish someday, Kif.

00:05:40.023 --> 00:05:41.525
Good hustle, soldier.

00:05:42.859 --> 00:05:44.569
Uh... Sorry, sir.

00:05:44.653 --> 00:05:46.446
I was still in attack mode.

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:48.365
You know how testosterone is.

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:52.077
As a bubbling crock-pot
of male hormones, I sure do.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.495
What's your name, private?

00:05:53.578 --> 00:05:56.498
Lee... la... man.

00:05:56.581 --> 00:05:57.624
La-man.

00:05:57.708 --> 00:05:58.709
Lemon!

00:05:58.792 --> 00:06:00.460
Lee Lemon, sir.

00:06:00.544 --> 00:06:02.379
Lemon, you're a man's man.

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:03.922
You're a man's man's man.

00:06:04.006 --> 00:06:05.173
And more importantly

00:06:05.257 --> 00:06:07.718
your hand, while firm and masculine

00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:09.761
is soft as a velvet child.

00:06:09.845 --> 00:06:11.096
What lotion do you use?

00:06:11.179 --> 00:06:12.764
Pert 'n' Popular, sir.

00:06:12.848 --> 00:06:13.849
Roger that.

00:06:13.932 --> 00:06:16.351
Kif, get me ten cases of Pert 'n' Popular.

00:06:16.435 --> 00:06:18.895
What shall I do with your Jergens, sir?

00:06:18.979 --> 00:06:21.356
Squirt it on some homeless man
with dry elbows.

00:06:22.232 --> 00:06:25.360
Private Lee Lemon may well be
the finest recruit I've seen

00:06:25.444 --> 00:06:27.195
in all my years of service.

00:06:27.279 --> 00:06:29.615
That young man fills me with hope...

00:06:29.948 --> 00:06:32.242
and some other emotions
that are weird and...

00:06:32.326 --> 00:06:33.535
deeply confusing me.

00:06:33.619 --> 00:06:34.661
Ew!

00:06:42.336 --> 00:06:43.337
Hello.

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:48.925
Mmm. Now that's a nice Rose.

00:06:49.009 --> 00:06:50.927
So, anyway, we open up the panda crate

00:06:51.011 --> 00:06:53.388
and wouldn't you know it,
the damn thing's dead.

00:06:53.472 --> 00:06:54.931
Upchucked its bamboo.

00:06:55.015 --> 00:06:56.058
True story.

00:06:56.183 --> 00:06:57.225
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

00:06:57.309 --> 00:06:59.353
That's
whatever-you-were-talking-about for you.

00:07:00.562 --> 00:07:03.482
- Mind if we sit with you?
- Uh... Hey.

00:07:03.565 --> 00:07:06.568
Why the hell would I? We're all guys here.

00:07:06.652 --> 00:07:09.071
Sweaty, hairy, gassy guys.

00:07:09.154 --> 00:07:10.739
Good point. I guess.

00:07:10.822 --> 00:07:12.950
You're my kind of soldier, Lemon...

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:17.871
a foul-mouthed, barrel-chested,
beer-belly pile of ugly muscle.

00:07:17.955 --> 00:07:21.333
So, any of you fellas
got a special lady back home?

00:07:21.416 --> 00:07:24.044
Well, I sort have a thing
for this girl I work with.

00:07:24.127 --> 00:07:25.128
Really?

00:07:25.212 --> 00:07:26.338
What type is she?

00:07:26.421 --> 00:07:29.257
You know, blonde, or Chinese, or Cyclops?

00:07:29.341 --> 00:07:30.425
Cyclops.

00:07:30.509 --> 00:07:33.011
Aw! She sounds sweet.

00:07:33.095 --> 00:07:35.389
But sweet girls aren't for you, eh?

00:07:35.472 --> 00:07:39.142
You hard-fightin', hard-fartin',
ugly, ugly son of a...

00:07:39.226 --> 00:07:41.979
- Stop! Stop flattering me.
- Ten-hut!

00:07:42.896 --> 00:07:46.191
Well, if it isn't Lee Lemon,

00:07:46.275 --> 00:07:49.736
the flaming star
of Brannigan's Rough Rangers.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:52.030
Say, Lemon, do you like to read?

00:07:52.114 --> 00:07:53.991
I just got a great book on tape.

00:07:54.074 --> 00:07:55.951
It's about life in ancient Greece and...

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.580
Sir, the alarm. I think I better...

00:08:00.664 --> 00:08:03.458
Shh. Don't talk. Just go.

00:08:09.089 --> 00:08:11.883
We are now in position above Spheron One.

00:08:11.967 --> 00:08:16.096
This is the moment we were training for
all yesterday afternoon.

00:08:16.179 --> 00:08:17.764
And now for the battle plan.

00:08:17.848 --> 00:08:18.849
As you all know

00:08:18.932 --> 00:08:21.810
the key to victory
is the element of surprise.

00:08:22.397 --> 00:08:23.398
Surprise!

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:37.993
It's creepy here.

00:08:38.076 --> 00:08:39.578
This is the worst part...

00:08:39.661 --> 00:08:41.622
the calm before the battle.

00:08:41.705 --> 00:08:43.206
And then the battle's not so bad?

00:08:43.373 --> 00:08:45.500
Right. I forgot about the battle.

00:08:48.629 --> 00:08:49.713
What's happening?

00:08:49.796 --> 00:08:52.049
Holy shoot! Looky!

00:08:52.132 --> 00:08:54.760
The enemy, they're balls!

00:09:01.475 --> 00:09:02.768
Charge your gun, Fry!

00:09:02.851 --> 00:09:03.977
Oh, right.

00:09:08.565 --> 00:09:11.568
Watch where you're shooting, private.
You spooked Felicity.

00:09:11.652 --> 00:09:13.236
There, there, boy.

00:09:23.705 --> 00:09:26.083
- Give this to my son.
- You got it.

00:09:26.166 --> 00:09:28.752
Wait. I didn't tell you where he lives.

00:09:28.835 --> 00:09:31.922
Hey, I think your son
might also like those boots.

00:09:38.095 --> 00:09:39.262
Cover us, buddy!

00:09:39.346 --> 00:09:41.932
You got the only wounded up
positron shooter.

00:09:49.898 --> 00:09:52.401
Fry, you emu-bellied coward!

00:09:52.526 --> 00:09:53.902
- Ah!
- Oh!

00:10:10.085 --> 00:10:11.253
Bender, no!

00:10:11.336 --> 00:10:13.714
If they put me on a stamp

00:10:13.797 --> 00:10:16.508
tell them to use the young Bender.

00:10:25.517 --> 00:10:26.768
Incoming wounded.

00:10:26.852 --> 00:10:29.354
All personnel report
to operating tent four.

00:10:29.438 --> 00:10:30.689
Repeat, four.

00:10:30.772 --> 00:10:31.940
I mean, five.

00:10:32.024 --> 00:10:33.317
Repeat, four.

00:10:34.484 --> 00:10:36.111
Are you ready to operate, doctor?

00:10:36.278 --> 00:10:39.031
I'd love to, but first
I have to perform surgery.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:41.825
I kid.

00:10:47.873 --> 00:10:48.915
Scalpel.

00:10:49.916 --> 00:10:50.917
Blood bucket.

00:10:51.835 --> 00:10:52.836
Priest.

00:10:52.919 --> 00:10:53.962
Next patient!

00:10:54.046 --> 00:10:56.048
Geez, Zoidberg, leave some
for the enemy to kill.

00:10:56.131 --> 00:10:57.591
Leave Dr. Zoidberg alone.

00:10:57.674 --> 00:10:59.343
He has twice the training you do.

00:10:59.426 --> 00:11:01.386
Yeah, he's a doctor and a butcher.

00:11:03.847 --> 00:11:05.265
See? This is how it starts...

00:11:05.349 --> 00:11:07.726
first with the jokes
then comes the heavy stuff.

00:11:09.728 --> 00:11:10.979
When will the killing end?

00:11:12.564 --> 00:11:14.399
Look at this sissy, Kif.

00:11:14.483 --> 00:11:16.652
While others were fighting
and dying pointlessly

00:11:16.735 --> 00:11:18.153
he was hiding in a hole

00:11:18.236 --> 00:11:20.656
wallowing in a pool of his own cowardice.

00:11:20.739 --> 00:11:21.907
That wasn't cowardice.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:24.076
I'm de-promoting you, soldier.

00:11:24.159 --> 00:11:27.162
Kif, what's the most
humiliating job there is?

00:11:27.245 --> 00:11:29.164
Being your assistant.

00:11:29.247 --> 00:11:31.750
Wrong. Being your assistant.

00:11:31.833 --> 00:11:35.587
Private Fry, you shall henceforth serve
as Kif's assistant.

00:11:35.671 --> 00:11:36.964
That doesn't sound too bad.

00:11:37.047 --> 00:11:39.257
You'll speak when I tell you to,
you filthy worm!

00:11:39.341 --> 00:11:41.259
I'm afraid he's gone.

00:11:41.593 --> 00:11:43.011
Doc, I ain't dead.

00:11:43.095 --> 00:11:46.056
Excuse me. I believe I'm the doctor.

00:11:46.139 --> 00:11:48.266
Believe it all you want.
That won't make it true.

00:11:50.143 --> 00:11:52.312
This isn't a war. It's a murder.

00:11:52.396 --> 00:11:54.356
This isn't a war. It's a murder.

00:11:56.525 --> 00:11:58.735
Bender, old buddy, hang in there.

00:12:02.698 --> 00:12:04.825
Here lies the bravest soldier I've seen

00:12:04.908 --> 00:12:06.743
since my mirror got grease on it.

00:12:06.827 --> 00:12:09.037
I hereby order that in Bender's honor

00:12:09.121 --> 00:12:11.832
he be melted down
and made into a statue of himself.

00:12:11.915 --> 00:12:13.500
Slow down there, Starsky.

00:12:13.583 --> 00:12:15.043
I'm up to something here.

00:12:15.127 --> 00:12:17.087
I want this robot fixed...

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:20.215
fixed like Kennedy fixed
the 1960 election.

00:12:20.299 --> 00:12:22.426
Damn bean-eating war hero.

00:12:22.509 --> 00:12:24.052
Are you ready to operate, doctor?

00:12:24.136 --> 00:12:26.513
I'd love to, but first
I have to perform surgery.

00:12:27.723 --> 00:12:29.182
That's my joke.

00:12:29.266 --> 00:12:30.601
I'll kill you!

00:12:38.358 --> 00:12:39.901
Prewar scotch.

00:12:43.196 --> 00:12:44.573
Welcome, lieutenant Bender.

00:12:44.656 --> 00:12:45.824
You're looking sharp.

00:12:45.907 --> 00:12:48.410
I got wheels with clickety clackers.

00:12:51.038 --> 00:12:53.165
Damn it, Kif, where's the little umbrella?

00:12:53.248 --> 00:12:55.751
That's what makes it
a scotch on the rocks.

00:12:55.834 --> 00:12:57.044
Actually, sir...

00:12:57.836 --> 00:12:59.087
Make me a new one.

00:13:01.506 --> 00:13:05.552
Use a brush, you dunderhead
and mix these mixed nuts.

00:13:05.636 --> 00:13:07.804
I see two almonds touching.

00:13:07.888 --> 00:13:09.139
Now listen here, Bender.

00:13:09.222 --> 00:13:12.392
This war is in danger
of going all quagmire on me.

00:13:12.476 --> 00:13:15.437
So, I'm sending you on one last mission.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:17.272
Hot diggity daffodil!

00:13:17.356 --> 00:13:19.691
- A mission of peace.
- Oh!

00:13:19.775 --> 00:13:22.569
You'll be negotiating
with the aliens' mysterious leaders,

00:13:22.653 --> 00:13:24.029
the Brain Balls.

00:13:24.112 --> 00:13:25.405
They've got a lot of brains

00:13:25.489 --> 00:13:27.491
and they've got a lot of chutzpah.

00:13:27.574 --> 00:13:30.369
Accompanying you will be
our top peace negotiator...

00:13:30.452 --> 00:13:31.995
Henry Kissinger.

00:13:32.079 --> 00:13:34.247
- How are you?
- Is he any good?

00:13:34.331 --> 00:13:37.709
Looking like that he talked his way
into Jill St. John's bed.

00:13:37.793 --> 00:13:38.794
'Nuff said.

00:13:43.173 --> 00:13:46.677
I'm so dizzy, my head is spinning

00:13:46.802 --> 00:13:49.888
Like a whirlpool, it never ends

00:13:50.222 --> 00:13:51.598
A little lower.

00:13:51.682 --> 00:13:52.849
Lower.

00:13:52.933 --> 00:13:54.142
Lower.

00:13:54.226 --> 00:13:55.602
A lot lower.

00:13:55.686 --> 00:13:56.937
Too low!

00:13:57.271 --> 00:13:58.438
Lower.

00:14:00.023 --> 00:14:02.651
I'm walkin' on sunshine

00:14:02.734 --> 00:14:04.152
Oh, oh, oh

00:14:08.282 --> 00:14:10.367
Private Lemon... no need to leave.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.577
My stall just became free.

00:14:12.869 --> 00:14:15.330
Maybe you should put on a towel, sir.

00:14:15.414 --> 00:14:16.957
Right.

00:14:18.917 --> 00:14:21.795
I'm about to try the new lotion
you recommended.

00:14:21.878 --> 00:14:24.423
If I should accidentally
put too much on my hands

00:14:24.506 --> 00:14:26.466
perhaps I could rub it onto you.

00:14:28.218 --> 00:14:29.553
Brannigan!

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.264
My God, cover yourself.

00:14:32.347 --> 00:14:34.016
I didn't live a thousand years

00:14:34.099 --> 00:14:35.726
and travel a quadrillion miles

00:14:35.809 --> 00:14:37.853
to look at another man's gizmo.

00:14:37.936 --> 00:14:39.605
Sorry, Mr. President.

00:14:39.688 --> 00:14:40.814
I didn't realize.

00:14:40.897 --> 00:14:43.275
Kif, raise him up about nipple high.

00:14:43.358 --> 00:14:46.445
Come on, Brannigan,
stuff yourself into a uniform.

00:14:46.528 --> 00:14:49.197
We've got to get off this planet
before the bomb goes off.

00:14:49.281 --> 00:14:50.365
Bomb?

00:14:50.449 --> 00:14:51.450
What bomb?

00:14:51.533 --> 00:14:53.035
The one we had the doctors implant

00:14:53.118 --> 00:14:54.703
in that gullible Bender robot.

00:14:59.374 --> 00:15:00.459
Mmm.

00:15:00.542 --> 00:15:01.835
Zapp. Zapp!

00:15:01.918 --> 00:15:03.378
Inspect the troops later.

00:15:03.462 --> 00:15:05.797
It's time to activate the bomb.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:13.013
Now as for economic cooperation...

00:15:13.347 --> 00:15:14.890
Oh! Excuse me.

00:15:23.565 --> 00:15:24.691
Attention...

00:15:24.775 --> 00:15:27.527
all personnel evacuate
the planet immediately.

00:15:27.611 --> 00:15:29.905
And not just becauseit's meat loaf night.

00:15:29.988 --> 00:15:32.491
Come along, Lemon,
before this whole dump blows up.

00:15:32.574 --> 00:15:33.992
Uh, Commander...

00:15:34.076 --> 00:15:36.036
could you tell me
when the bomb is exploding?

00:15:36.119 --> 00:15:38.372
Of course, my significant soldier.

00:15:38.455 --> 00:15:39.957
The bomb is voice activated.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:41.375
It will detonate the instant

00:15:41.458 --> 00:15:44.127
the robot unwittingly speaks
a certain word.

00:15:44.211 --> 00:15:46.088
What's the word... Sir?

00:15:46.171 --> 00:15:49.257
It's the one word the robot uses
more than any other.

00:15:49.341 --> 00:15:51.343
We got it from this convenient database

00:15:51.426 --> 00:15:54.262
of his ten most frequently used words.

00:15:58.558 --> 00:16:00.435
Number ten, chump.

00:16:00.519 --> 00:16:02.479
Number nine, chumpette.

00:16:02.562 --> 00:16:04.898
Number eight, yours.

00:16:04.982 --> 00:16:06.858
Number seven, up.

00:16:06.942 --> 00:16:09.611
Number six, pimpmobile.

00:16:09.695 --> 00:16:11.405
Number five, bite.

00:16:11.488 --> 00:16:13.573
Number four, my.

00:16:13.824 --> 00:16:16.159
Number three, shiny.

00:16:16.243 --> 00:16:18.578
Number two, daffodil.

00:16:18.662 --> 00:16:21.915
And Bender's number one
most frequently uttered word

00:16:21.999 --> 00:16:25.085
the word which, if uttered,
will blow up this entire planet...

00:16:25.752 --> 00:16:26.878
Ass.

00:16:27.087 --> 00:16:28.755
We don't have long.

00:16:29.006 --> 00:16:31.508
We demand bouncing, followed by rolling,

00:16:31.591 --> 00:16:33.385
followed by rolling of the third type.

00:16:33.468 --> 00:16:34.469
Say what?

00:16:34.553 --> 00:16:36.305
My chair's too hard.

00:16:36.388 --> 00:16:37.472
It's a real pain in the...

00:16:37.556 --> 00:16:38.932
What do you call it?

00:16:39.391 --> 00:16:40.434
Lower back.

00:16:40.517 --> 00:16:41.727
Yeah, that whole region.

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:55.574
Okay. I got to break down that gate

00:16:55.657 --> 00:16:57.701
beat up those three guards,
steal that chopper

00:16:57.784 --> 00:16:58.869
and rescue Bender.

00:17:01.913 --> 00:17:03.248
Hey, I did it.

00:17:03.332 --> 00:17:04.625
Wait, that's not me.

00:17:04.708 --> 00:17:07.002
Come on, we got to save Bender.

00:17:07.628 --> 00:17:09.171
You want to save him, too, Lemon?

00:17:09.254 --> 00:17:10.297
You barely know him.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.424
Fry, don't you recognize me?

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:14.051
Hermes?

00:17:14.134 --> 00:17:16.178
Lee... when will I see you again?

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:20.766
The two of you are... good friends?

00:17:20.849 --> 00:17:23.602
But I thought we would be... good friends.

00:17:23.936 --> 00:17:28.607
Well, let's see how friendly you get
when you're sharing a prison cell.

00:17:34.947 --> 00:17:35.948
Hey, Zapp.

00:17:37.699 --> 00:17:38.700
- Leela!
- Leela.

00:17:38.784 --> 00:17:40.869
So it's you I've been attracted to.

00:17:40.953 --> 00:17:44.873
Oh, God, I've never been so happy
to be beaten up by a woman.

00:17:44.957 --> 00:17:46.458
Let's do it again sometime.

00:17:49.378 --> 00:17:52.464
The elders tell of
a young ball much like you.

00:17:52.547 --> 00:17:54.716
He bounced three meters in the air.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.427
Then, he bounced 1.8 meters in the air.

00:17:57.511 --> 00:18:00.973
Then, he bounced four meters in the air.

00:18:01.056 --> 00:18:02.557
Do I make myself clear?

00:18:02.641 --> 00:18:06.561
Mr. Ambassador,
our people tell the same story.

00:18:08.855 --> 00:18:11.275
These balls are making me testy!

00:18:11.358 --> 00:18:13.443
If they don't stop bouncing and jiggling

00:18:13.527 --> 00:18:16.238
I swear I'm going to shove
this treaty up their...

00:18:16.321 --> 00:18:17.572
Wait a second.

00:18:17.656 --> 00:18:19.199
Where do you shove things up a ball?

00:18:19.283 --> 00:18:21.618
This isn't a productive area
of discussion.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:26.123
We're here.

00:18:26.206 --> 00:18:27.749
I followed the bouncing balls.

00:18:27.833 --> 00:18:31.420
I'll keep the chopper at a safe altitude
while you parachute down.

00:18:31.503 --> 00:18:32.754
Okay.

00:18:32.838 --> 00:18:34.756
My best friend's life is at stake.

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:36.842
I can finally prove that I'm not a coward.

00:18:38.552 --> 00:18:39.720
Will you push me?

00:18:39.803 --> 00:18:41.179
I already did.

00:18:41.513 --> 00:18:43.348
Thank you!

00:18:53.609 --> 00:18:57.029
At last... war has made me into a man.

00:18:57.487 --> 00:18:59.072
Whee!

00:18:59.948 --> 00:19:01.533
Please, gentlemen

00:19:01.617 --> 00:19:03.827
we must put an end to the bloodshed.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:07.205
We have all seen too many
body bags and ball sacks.

00:19:07.289 --> 00:19:10.792
We cannot condone bouncing
of the seventh variety.

00:19:10.876 --> 00:19:12.127
Enough of this crap!

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:14.755
I'm catching the next pimpmobile
out of here

00:19:14.838 --> 00:19:18.467
but before I go, I have one thing to say.

00:19:19.051 --> 00:19:22.971
Bite my shiny... metal...

00:19:23.055 --> 00:19:24.931
Stop! You can't say the next word.

00:19:25.015 --> 00:19:26.224
Up yours, chump.

00:19:26.308 --> 00:19:28.852
I said it 906 times before lunch.

00:19:28.936 --> 00:19:30.938
Bender, if you say the "a" word

00:19:31.021 --> 00:19:33.732
you'll blow this whole planet
straight to the "h" word.

00:19:37.152 --> 00:19:40.030
Young man...
you have the bravery of a hero

00:19:40.113 --> 00:19:42.324
and breath as fresh as a summer ham.

00:19:51.541 --> 00:19:52.626
What? What is funny?

00:19:52.709 --> 00:19:55.003
Bender's got the upper hand now.

00:19:55.087 --> 00:19:57.631
The name of the game is make Bender happy

00:19:57.714 --> 00:19:59.299
or he blows up the planet!

00:20:00.258 --> 00:20:02.386
I'd rather die and take everybody with me

00:20:02.469 --> 00:20:03.971
than sit here one more minute

00:20:04.054 --> 00:20:06.390
and listen to these idiots talk
about bouncing.

00:20:06.473 --> 00:20:07.683
Please, stay calm.

00:20:07.766 --> 00:20:09.601
There's no need to bounce off the handle.

00:20:09.685 --> 00:20:11.270
That's it, I'm saying it!

00:20:11.353 --> 00:20:12.854
- "A" is for a...
- Wait!

00:20:12.938 --> 00:20:15.357
Stop. We give in
to all of Earth's demands.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:16.483
The war is over.

00:20:16.566 --> 00:20:18.318
Our home planet is yours.

00:20:18.402 --> 00:20:19.861
All right!

00:20:20.112 --> 00:20:21.280
Hey, wait a minute.

00:20:21.363 --> 00:20:22.739
This is your home planet?

00:20:22.823 --> 00:20:24.491
We're the evil invading aliens?

00:20:24.574 --> 00:20:25.575
Correct.

00:20:25.659 --> 00:20:28.328
Then I guess you learned
a valuable lesson.

00:20:28.412 --> 00:20:30.330
Don't mess with Earth.

00:20:30.414 --> 00:20:31.915
May you bounce in peace.

00:20:31.999 --> 00:20:34.293
Get the hell off my planet.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:48.265
Well, that's it.

00:20:48.348 --> 00:20:50.309
Let's reactivate him.

00:20:50.392 --> 00:20:51.560
Wake up!

00:20:54.062 --> 00:20:55.772
Hey, chumps and chumpettes.

00:20:55.856 --> 00:20:57.190
Did you get the bomb out?

00:20:57.274 --> 00:21:00.068
Can I go back to saying
the word I love to say?

00:21:00.152 --> 00:21:02.279
I'm sorry, but we couldn't remove it.

00:21:02.362 --> 00:21:04.364
It's stuck in there
with glue or something.

00:21:04.448 --> 00:21:05.490
I don't know.

00:21:05.574 --> 00:21:07.492
Well, this is just great.

00:21:07.576 --> 00:21:09.995
What's the point of living
if I can't say ass?

00:21:11.455 --> 00:21:13.165
Hey, I didn't blow up!

00:21:13.248 --> 00:21:14.791
Ass!

00:21:14.875 --> 00:21:17.252
All right! I'm back in the saddle.

00:21:17.336 --> 00:21:18.670
We couldn't disarm the bomb

00:21:18.754 --> 00:21:20.547
so we reset the word that triggers it.

00:21:20.631 --> 00:21:22.883
It's from the list of words
you almost never say.

00:21:22.966 --> 00:21:24.551
That's using your ass.

00:21:24.635 --> 00:21:25.636
So what's the word?

00:21:25.719 --> 00:21:27.429
We think it's better if you don't know.

00:21:27.971 --> 00:21:29.139
Oh, come on.

00:21:29.222 --> 00:21:31.350
I'm not going to say it. Please?

00:21:31.683 --> 00:21:33.268
- Is it "please"?
- Nope.

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:35.896
Hmm. Words I never say.

00:21:35.979 --> 00:21:37.981
Oh, I know. "Thanks."

00:21:38.065 --> 00:21:40.567
Bender, stop trying to destroy the world.

00:21:40.651 --> 00:21:43.445
Wait. Is it "sorry"? No.

00:21:43.528 --> 00:21:44.738
"Funderful"?

00:21:45.572 --> 00:21:46.949
"Non-alcoholic"?

00:21:47.032 --> 00:21:48.825
- Stop it, mon.
- Quit it.

00:21:48.909 --> 00:21:51.078
"Compassion"? "Shrimp toast"?

00:21:51.578 --> 00:21:52.663
"Antiquing"?

00:21:54.539 --> 00:21:55.582
I'm all right.